1.1.text:
Article 7
Prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women is intended to create a safe environment for women and to reduce the vulnerability to violence, exploitation and discrimination of vulnerable groups of women, as follows:
a. women in disaster and social conflict situations; b. women with disabilities; c. women with HIV/AIDS;
d. women migrant workers;
e. girls;
f. women heads of household;
g. domestic women workers;
h. home-based women workers;
i. elderly women;
j. informal women workers;
k. women in situations of intolerance; and
l. other vulnerable groups of women.

Article 12
(1) Forms of protection services for women victims of violence, exploitation and discrimination, include services:
a. complaints;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. reproductive health;
d. social rehabilitation;
e. social reintegration; and
f. legal assistance and accompaniment.
(2) Services for women victims are implemented quickly, comprehensively, with quality and integrated with services provided by the City Regional Government, community, educational institutions, boarding educational institutions, religious institutions, professional institutions, business sector through an integrated service system.

CHAPTER IX
OBLIGATIONS OF THE CITY REGIONAL GOVERNMENT
Article 30
(1) The obligations of the City Regional Government in the implementation of Women's Protection, are as follows: a. formulate policies and include Women's Protection programs in regional development planning and budgeting;
b. provide complaint services, health, social rehabilitation, legal assistance and enforcement as well as repatriation and social reintegration for women victims;
c. establish shelter services and/or safe houses; d. establish special mechanisms for integrated hospital-based services;
e. establish PPT;
f. establish UPT for Women and Children Protection; g. formulate standard operating procedures and service referral systems;
- 16 -
h. conduct prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women;
i. provide human resources and infrastructure facilities for Women's Protection;
j. increase support and develop women's protection service institutions owned by the City Regional Government and the community;
k. develop victim services based on communities, boarding educational institutions, basic educational institutions, religious institutions, and the business sector;
l. conduct capacity building;
m. conduct coordination and cooperation;
n. conduct empowerment to increase community participation;
o. develop an integrated data and information system for women's protection; p. conduct control, guidance and supervision of the implementation of women's protection administration; and
q. provide awards to the community, community organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, boarding educational institutions, the business sector and other parties.
(2) The planning and budgeting of Women's Protection as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a, shall be the responsibility of Regional Apparatus implementing supporting functions of Government Affairs and the Agency.

Article 8
(1) Prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women, is carried out in the following fields:
a. education;
b. health;
c. religion;
d. security;
e. justice;
f. public works and spatial planning;
g. public housing and residential areas; h. social affairs;
- 8 -
i. labor;
j. women's empowerment and child protection; k. defense;
l. environment;
m. population administration and civil registration; n. population control and family planning; o. transportation;
p. communication and informatics;
q. cooperatives, small and medium enterprises;
r. youth and sports;
s. culture;
t. tourism;
u. trade and industry; and
v. other fields.
(2) Prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out by:
a. developing media for communication, information, education and public campaigns through media;
b. developing educational materials and curriculum in accordance with regional authority;
c. developing safe transportation systems and public spaces;
d. building early detection systems, security and integrated complaint services in industrial areas, companies, residential areas, educational environments, boarding educational environments, and other public spaces;
e. implementing consultation services for families, prospective brides and grooms, students, Islamic students, youth, university students and vulnerable groups;
f. encouraging behavioral change of parents and society;
g. developing regional policies, schools, boarding schools, and universities that are safe and friendly for women and integrated with regional spatial planning policies;
h. establishing and developing cadres, communities, young people, students, Islamic students, university students, journalists, social media influencers, educators, community leaders and religious leaders for prevention;
i. conducting education and advocacy to owners, managers and/or users of social media;
j. developing protection systems and special support for vulnerable women groups;
k. conducting awareness-raising for perpetrators;
l. increasing the capacity of City Regional Government, government agencies, educational institutions, religious institutions, health service provider institutions, professional institutions, business sector, service institutions, youth organizations, legal aid organizations, media, religious leaders, community leaders and communities;
m. conducting cooperation with religious institutions, community social institutions, service institutions, - 9 - universities, media, youth organizations, religious leaders and community leaders; and
n. conducting socialization of laws and regulations. (3) The fields and forms of prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) are implemented by agencies, regional apparatus, institutions, community institutions, organizations, communities, professional institutions that handle related affairs in accordance with their authority based on the provisions of laws and regulations.

CHAPTER VI
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 23
(1) The City Regional Government has the obligation to strengthen community participation in the implementation of women's protection.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be conducted in the form of:
a. prevention;
b. services and referral;
c. development of information data systems;
d. strengthening of service institutions;
e. research and policy advocacy;
f. control, guidance and supervision; and g. financing.
(3) Strengthening of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), may be conducted through:
a. strengthening cooperation; and
b. strengthening institutional capacity for prevention and services from the community, boarding educational institutions, and the business sector.
(4) The business sector has responsibility in the implementation of Women's Protection in accordance with the objectives of Corporate Social and Environmental Responsibility.
- 14 - (5) The form of business sector responsibility as referred to in paragraph (4), shall be conducted as follows: a. financial assistance to service institutions; b. empowerment;
c. capacity building;
d. publication and information media;
e. provision of facilities and infrastructure;
f. establishment of special institutions for prevention and services for violence complaints; and
g. social assistance that is non-binding.

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD,
THE MAYOR OF CIREBON,
Considering : a. that every woman has the right to obtain a sense of security and protection from all forms of violence, exploitation, torture, discrimination, and other mistreatment that degrades human dignity and violates human rights;
b. that to ensure the prevention and handling of acts of violence against women in a fast, accurate, comprehensive, and integrated manner, regulation regarding the protection of women is required;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women from Violence, Exploitation and Discrimination;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95);
3. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning the Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635), as amended by Law Number 31 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning the Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 293, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5602);
4. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
5. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic - 2 - of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587), as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 6 of 2023 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);
6. Law Number 30 of 2014 concerning Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 292, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5601), as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 6 of 2023 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);
7. Law Number 12 of 2022 concerning the Criminal Act of Sexual Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 120, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6792);
8. Law Number 17 of 2023 concerning Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2023 Number 105, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6887);
9. Law Number 108 of 2024 concerning the City of Cirebon in the Province of West Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2024 Number 294, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 7045);
10. Government Regulation Number 28 of 2024 concerning the Implementing Regulation of Law Number 17 of 2023 concerning Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2024 Number 135, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6952);
11. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 4 of 2023 concerning Acting Governor, Acting Regent, and Acting Mayor (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2023 Number 310);
12. Decree of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 100.2.1.3-6572 of 2023 concerning the Appointment of Acting Mayor of Cirebon, Province of West Java;
13. Regional Regulation of the City of Cirebon Number 9 of 2016 concerning the Establishment of Regional Legal Products (Regional Gazette of the City of Cirebon Year 2016 Number 9), as amended by Regional Regulation of the City of Cirebon Number 5 of 2020 concerning Amendment to Regional Regulation Number 9 of 2016 concerning the Establishment of Regional Legal Products (Regional Gazette of the City of Cirebon Year 2020 Number 5);
14. Regional Regulation of the City of Cirebon Number 5 of 2021 concerning the Establishment and Composition of Regional Apparatus of the City of Cirebon (Regional Gazette of the City of Cirebon - 3 - Year 2021 Number 5, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of the City of Cirebon Number 107);
15. Regional Regulation of the City of Cirebon Number 3 of 2023 concerning Government Affairs Administered by the Regional Government of the City of Cirebon (Regional Gazette of the City of Cirebon Year 2023 Number 3, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of the City of Cirebon Number 128);
With Mutual Approval

Article 3
The Protection of Women aims to:
a. prevent all forms of violence, exploitation, and discrimination against women;
b. provide services and recovery for women victims of violence, exploitation and discrimination;
c. realize the capacity of the City Regional Government in implementing the Protection of Women from violence, exploitation and discrimination;
d. increase community participation in the Protection of Women; and
e. realize a social life that is safe and free from all forms of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women.

